empty: branches: 0 next=1
== three branches at one point ==
branches: 3 next=4
    br-1 Baseline @sec-3
    br-2 Robust @sec-3
    br-3 No Outliers @sec-3
== exactly one is selected at a point ==
-> select Robust: selected br-2
branches: 3 next=4
    br-1 Baseline @sec-3
  * br-2 Robust @sec-3
    br-3 No Outliers @sec-3
-> select No Outliers: selected br-3
branches: 3 next=4
    br-1 Baseline @sec-3
    br-2 Robust @sec-3
  * br-3 No Outliers @sec-3
selected at the point: br-3
== nesting: a branch point inside a branch ==
-> select Inner: selected br-4
branches: 4 next=5
    br-1 Baseline @sec-3
    br-2 Robust @sec-3
  * br-3 No Outliers @sec-3
    * br-4 Inner @sec-1 under br-3
== rename ==
-> rename: renamed br-2
-> rename to nothing: invalid empty
-> rename a branch that is not there: unknown br-99
branches: 4 next=5
    br-1 Baseline @sec-3
    br-2 Robust v2 @sec-3
  * br-3 No Outliers @sec-3
    * br-4 Inner @sec-1 under br-3
== deleting a branch takes its descendants with it ==
-> delete No Outliers: removed 2
branches: 2 next=5
    br-1 Baseline @sec-3
    br-2 Robust v2 @sec-3
the point falls back to baseline: []
